      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- SE_PERSON\n- MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS\n\n## Column Mapping\n- employee type: SE_PERSON.EMPLOYEE_TYPE\n- Student: SE_PERSON.EMPLOYEE_TYPE\n- department 6: MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT\n- department name: MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- Electrical Eng & Computer Sci: MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- MIT ID: SE_PERSON.MIT_ID\n- full name: SE_PERSON.FULL_NAME, MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.FULL_NAME\n- student year: MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.STUDENT_YEAR\n- total units: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\n- regular academic terms: ACADEMIC_TERMS.IS_REGULAR_TERM\n- Mathematics: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n\n## Join Keys\n- MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.FULL_NAME <-> SE_PERSON.FULL_NAME\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE\n\n## Question\nFor students whose employee type is 'Student', who are in department 6 (Electrical Engineering and Computer Science), and whose department name is 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci', show their MIT ID, full name, department name, student year, the running sum of MIT IDs within each student year group ordered by MIT ID, and the coefficient of variation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered in regular academic terms in their department (excluding 'Mathematics'). Do not return any rounded answers."
