      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"entities\": [{\"columns\": [\"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\", \"CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS\", \"DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Source process\", \"detail\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS is the catalog-declared unit value per offering; SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS and SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS are registrar subject-level values; CIS/DRUPAL catalog feeds carry their own copies\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Companion unit columns\", \"detail\": \"All these tables also expose LECTURE_UNITS, LAB_UNITS, and preparation units (PREPARATION_UNITS except SUBJECT_SUMMARY which uses PREP_UNITS); DESIGN_UNITS exists in COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, CIS and DRUPAL catalogs but not in SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Variability flag\", \"detail\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.IS_VARIABLE_UNITS marks subjects whose units vary; analyses of fixed-unit statistics typically filter IS_VARIABLE_UNITS='N'\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Unit statistics (avg/stddev/variance/geometric mean) over catalog offerings, optionally split by lecture/lab/design or filtered by variable-units flag\": \"Use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS with its companion unit columns.\", \"Unit statistics tied to actual enrollment records or subject groups per term\": \"Use SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS.\", \"Unit statistics at subject-offering rollup level with offering department/school\": \"Use SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS.\", \"Fixed-unit analyses excluding variable-unit subjects\": \"Filter COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.IS_VARIABLE_UNITS = 'N'.\"}, \"desc\": \"Total credit unit columns replicated across catalog and registrar subject tables. They represent the same business quantity (total credit units of a subject) but come from different processes and pair with different companion unit columns.\", \"id\": \"column_concept_total_units\", \"name\": \"Total Credit Units\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_department_name\", \"name\": \"Department Name\", \"desc\": \"Department name columns across subject offering, catalog, lookup, employee, and library reserve instructor tables. Two academic naming conventions exist (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME) with the same academic value domain; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT also holds academic departments but in a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME shares the column name but holds the HR organizational unit name (different value domain). Choosing the right one depends on the table family, the value format, whether the department is the catalog owner or the actual offering department, and whether an academic or HR department is meant.\", \"columns\": [\"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT\", \"MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Naming convention\", \"detail\": \"DEPARTMENT_NAME is used by catalog/summary tables (COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_SUMMARY), department/course lookup tables, and the student directory (MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY); OFFER_DEPT_NAME is used by offering/program tables (SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED) and denotes the department that actually offers the subject; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR uses the plain column name DEPARTMENT for the course's academic department; SE_PERSON uses ORGANIZATION for the person's organizational unit\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Value format\", \"detail\": \"Catalog, summary, offering, student-directory, and lookup tables store plain department names (e.g. 'Mathematics', 'Chemistry', 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'); LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT stores a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics', '06 - Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'), with some unprefixed values (e.g. 'Architecture'), so it is not directly comparable to plain-name columns without stripping the prefix\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Academic vs HR/organization value domain\", \"detail\": \"Catalog, summary, offering, library, student-directory, and lookup tables share the academic department domain; EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME is the HR organizational unit name and has a different domain (e.g. 'Lincoln Laboratory', 'Department of Physics'), where some values coincide with academic names but many do not, and some carry a 'Department of ...' prefix; SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION holds organizational unit names that may use different naming variants than the academic domain for the same unit (e.g. 'Electrical Engineering-Computer Science' vs the academic 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'), so equality filters across the two conventions must use each table's own variant\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Companion code column\", \"detail\": \"Catalog/summary tables carry DEPARTMENT_CODE joining SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE; offering/program tables carry OFFER_DEPT_CODE joining SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE or STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE; MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY carries DEPARTMENT (the academic department code) joining SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, which is the reliable join key instead of the name; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR has no department code column, only the prefixed name text; EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY carries DEPARTMENT_NUMBER (HR department number) and SE_PERSON carries no department code, neither joining to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Filtering subjects by department in catalog or summary analysis\": \"Use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME or SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME.\", \"Filtering by department in section-level, textbook-program, or library analysis\": \"Use the OFFER_DEPT_NAME column of SUBJECT_OFFERED / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY / TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED / LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.\", \"Joining fact tables to department dimension attributes (school, full name, degree-granting)\": \"Prefer code joins: DEPARTMENT_CODE / OFFER_DEPT_CODE = SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE; name equality joins are used when codes are unavailable.\", \"Matching departments across a DEPARTMENT_NAME table and an OFFER_DEPT_NAME table\": \"The values are directly comparable (same academic name domain), e.g. joining SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME to TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME.\", \"Filtering employees by their HR organizational unit (e.g. names containing 'Department', or HR units like 'Political Science')\": \"Use EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME; do not join it to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, and pair it with DEPARTMENT_NUMBER for HR grouping.\", \"Filtering by department in section-level, textbook-program, or library subject analysis\": \"Use the OFFER_DEPT_NAME column of SUBJECT_OFFERED / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY / TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED / LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.\", \"Filtering library reserve course instructors by academic department or library unit\": \"Use LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT with the prefixed value format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); do not compare it directly to plain department-name columns.\", \"Filtering students by their academic department\": \"Use MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT (code) joined to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE for reliable matching, or MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME for direct name filters; the name shares the academic domain with SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME.\", \"Filtering a person master (SE_PERSON) record by organizational unit such as an academic department\": \"Use SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION with its own naming variant (e.g. 'Electrical Engineering-Computer Science'); do not equate it directly to MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME or SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, which use the academic variant (e.g. 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci').\"}}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_term_code\", \"name\": \"Term Code\", \"desc\": \"Term code columns in YYYYTT format (e.g. '2025FA', '2019SP', '2021JA', '2012SU'; TT = FA Fall, SP Spring, JA January/IAP, SU Summer) appearing across term dimension and fact tables. They are the universal join key linking subject offerings, textbook materials, library reserves, and IAP activities to term attributes.\", \"columns\": [\"ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE\", \"ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER.TERM_CODE\", \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\", \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TERM_CODE\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TERM_CODE\", \"TIP_DETAIL.TERM_CODE\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\", \"LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.TERM_CODE\", \"IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.TERM_CODE\", \"TIME_DAY.ACADEMIC_TERM_CODE\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Semantics\", \"TERM_CODE (fact tables)\": \"The term in which the offering/material/activity record exists\", \"EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE (COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED)\": \"The term from which the catalog attributes take effect; may differ from the record's TERM_CODE\", \"TIME_DAY.ACADEMIC_TERM_CODE\": \"The academic term a calendar day belongs to\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Join behavior\", \"TERM_CODE\": \"Direct equality join between fact tables and ACADEMIC_TERMS/ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\", \"EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE\": \"Joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE when catalog attributes must be evaluated as of the term they became effective\", \"ACADEMIC_TERM_CODE\": \"Joined to term tables' TERM_CODE or to fact tables' TERM_CODE for calendar attributes\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Filtering subject offerings by the term they are offered in\": \"Use the fact table's TERM_CODE.\", \"Filtering catalog attributes by when they took effect (e.g. regular-term status of the effective term)\": \"Use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE.\", \"Attaching calendar day attributes (day of week, fiscal year) to terms or IAP activities\": \"Use TIME_DAY.ACADEMIC_TERM_CODE or TIME_DAY.CALENDAR_DATE = TERM_START_DATE.\", \"Resolving 'current/previous/upcoming term' references\": \"Use ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER.TERM_CODE with TERM_INDICATOR.\"}}], \"not_found\": []}"
