      "content": "The database is persistently inaccessible (MySQL error 1045 — access denied), so verification via `mysql_query` is impossible. I'll finalize based on the semantic-network evidence and metric precedents.\n\n---\n\n# Report\n\n## 1. Entity Semantics\n\n### Tables\n\n**`SE_PERSON`** — Person master table keyed by `MIT_ID`. One row per person. Key columns retrieved: `MIT_ID` (\"Unique institute person identifier\"), `FULL_NAME` (\"Full name\"), `EMPLOYEE_TYPE` (\"Employee type classification\"), plus `KRB_NAME`, `PAYROLL_RANK`, `POSITION_TITLE`, `IS_ACTIVE`, `OFFICE_LOCATION`, `ORGANIZATION`, `FIRST_NAME`, `LAST_NAME`, `MIDDLE_NAME`, `WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE`. This is the **only** table in the discovered set carrying `EMPLOYEE_TYPE`.\n\n**`MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY`** — Student directory, one row per student. Key columns: `FULL_NAME` (\"Full name in 'Last, First M.' format\"), `DEPARTMENT` (\"Academic department code the student belongs to; joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"), `DEPARTMENT_NAME` (\"Academic department name of the student, e.g. 'Materials Science and Eng', **'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci**'\"), `STUDENT_YEAR` (\"Student year/level code, e.g. 'G' for graduate\"), plus name components, `OFFICE_LOCATION`, `OFFICE_PHONE`, `EMAIL_ADDRESS`, `FULL_NAME_UPPERCASE`, `WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE`. This is the **only** table carrying `STUDENT_YEAR` and the student's academic `DEPARTMENT` code.\n\n**`COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED`** — Course-catalog subject offering, one row per subject offering per term/academic year. Key columns for this task: `TOTAL_UNITS` (\"Total credit units of the subject (lecture+lab+preparation unless variable)\"), `DEPARTMENT_NAME` (\"Offering department name, e.g. 'Mathematics', 'Chemistry'\"), `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `TERM_CODE` (\"Term code of the offering record in YYYYTT format\"), `EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE` (\"Term code from which the catalog attributes of this subject take effect; **frequently joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE for term-status filtering**\").\n\n**`ACADEMIC_TERMS`** — Academic term dimension, one row per term. Key column: `IS_REGULAR_TERM` (\"'Y'/'N' flag indicating a regular term (Fall/Spring) versus non-regular terms (Summer, January/IAP); **only present in ACADEMIC_TERMS, not in ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL**\"), plus `TERM_CODE`, `TERM_DESCRIPTION`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `TERM_STATUS_INDICATOR`, `IS_CURRENT_TERM`.\n\n### Concepts\n- **`concept_person_directory`** — groups `SE_PERSON`, `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY`, `EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY`, `DRUPAL_EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY`, `HR_FACULTY_ROSTER`, `OPA_PERSON_CURRENT`. States they \"jointly answer questions about who a person is … and whether they are employee, faculty, or student.\"\n- **`concept_subject_offering_facts`** — groups `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED` with registrar/TIP/library offering facts; notes they \"share subject identity (SUBJECT_ID, TERM_CODE) and department attribution but differ in granularity, enrollment semantics, and available measures.\"\n- **`concept_academic_term_dimension`** — groups `ACADEMIC_TERMS`, `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL`, `ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER`; \"Coverage differs: the full historical term list, the status-tracked term subset, and the three-row relative term parameter reference.\"\n- **`concept_course_catalog_sources`** — groups `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED`, `CIS_COURSE_CATALOG`, `DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG`.\n- **`concept_department_dimension`** — `SIS_DEPARTMENT`, `STUDENT_DEPARTMENT`, `SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT`.\n\n### Column Concepts\n- **`column_concept_total_units`** — members: `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS`, `SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS`, `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS`, `CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS`, `DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS`. Decision guide: *\"Unit statistics (avg/stddev/variance/geometric mean) over catalog offerings … → Use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS with its companion unit columns.\"*\n- **`column_concept_department_name`** — 14 member columns including `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION`. Critical comparison: *\"SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION holds organizational unit names that may use different naming variants … (e.g. 'Electrical Engineering-Computer Science' vs the academic 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'), so equality filters across the two conventions must use each table's own variant.\"* Decision guide: *\"Filtering students by their academic department → Use MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT (code) … or MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME for direct name filters.\"*\n- **`column_concept_term_code`** — includes both `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE` and `.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE`. Comparison: *\"TERM_CODE (fact tables): The term in which the offering/material/activity record exists; EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE: The term from which the catalog attributes take effect; may differ from the record's TERM_CODE.\"* Decision guide: *\"Filtering catalog attributes by when they took effect (**e.g. regular-term status of the effective term**) → Use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE.\"*\n\n### Metrics (precedents examined in full)\n`dw_2759`, `dw_463`, `dw_2240`, `dw_1983`, `dw_4640`, `dw_2180`, `dw_1049`, `dw_3417`, `dw_3294`, `dw_359`, `dw_4061`, `dw_3664`, `dw_4387`, `dw_3248`, `dw_4701`, `dw_2597`, `dw_41`, `dw_1471`, `dw_1335`, `dw_1212`, `dw_3530`, `dw_3684`, `dw_3867`.\n\n## 2. Lineage & Relationships\n\n**`SE_PERSON`** (`semantic_graph query_neighbors`, both): outgoing `joins` → `EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY`, `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY`; incoming `joins` ← `LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR` (via `INSTRUCTOR_NAME = SE_PERSON.FULL_NAME`); incoming `concept` ← `concept_person_directory`; incoming `column_concept` ← `column_concept_department_name`, `column_concept_office_location`. **The `SE_PERSON ↔ MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY` join edge is explicitly documented in the graph**, confirming the hint's `FULL_NAME` join key.\n\n**`COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED`** (`query_neighbors`, relation_type=joins, both): outgoing → `ACADEMIC_TERMS`, `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL`, `SIS_SUBJECT_CODE`, `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION`, `SIS_DEPARTMENT`, `FCLT_ROOMS`, `EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY`, `CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE`, `SUBJECT_ATTRIBUTE`; incoming ← `SUBJECT_SUMMARY`, `TIP_DETAIL`, `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED`, `IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL`, `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED`, `SUBJECT_OFFERED`, `CIS_COURSE_CATALOG`, `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY`, and a self-edge. `metrics_by_table` returned **61 dependent metrics**.\n\n**`ACADEMIC_TERMS`** — member of `concept_academic_term_dimension`; joined from `TIME_MONTH` via `ACADEMIC_TERM = TERM_CODE`; sole holder of `IS_REGULAR_TERM`.\n\n**`MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY`** — member of `concept_person_directory`; `DEPARTMENT` joins `SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE`; joined from `SE_PERSON` on `FULL_NAME`.\n\n## 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n### 3a. Objective dimension matrix\n\n| Dimension | `SE_PERSON` | `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY` | `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED` | `ACADEMIC_TERMS` |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | one row per person (retrieved `default_granularity`) | one row per student (retrieved) | one row per subject offering per term/academic year (retrieved) | one row per academic term (retrieved) |\n| Has `EMPLOYEE_TYPE` | **YES** (column def: \"Employee type classification\") | NO (absent from retrieved column list) | NO | NO |\n| Has `STUDENT_YEAR` | NO | **YES** (\"Student year/level code, e.g. 'G'\") | NO | NO |\n| Has `MIT_ID` | **YES** (\"Unique institute person identifier\") | NO (absent from retrieved column list) | NO (has `RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID`) | NO |\n| Academic dept name | NO — has `ORGANIZATION` with a **different naming variant** ('Electrical Engineering-Computer Science'), per `column_concept_department_name` comparison | **YES** `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, value domain includes 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci' (column def) | **YES** `DEPARTMENT_NAME` (\"Offering department name, e.g. 'Mathematics'\") | NO |\n| Academic dept code | NO (\"SE_PERSON carries no department code\" — `column_concept_department_name` comparison) | **YES** `DEPARTMENT` | **YES** `DEPARTMENT_CODE` | NO |\n| Has `TOTAL_UNITS` | NO | NO | **YES** | NO |\n| Has `IS_REGULAR_TERM` | NO | NO | NO | **YES** — \"only present in ACADEMIC_TERMS, not in ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\" (column def) |\n| Join/fan-out risk | `FULL_NAME` is not declared unique; `dw_463` precedent applies `MIN(sp.MIT_ID)` + `GROUP BY sp.FULL_NAME`, evidencing possible multi-row names | one row per student (retrieved granularity) | many rows per department (one per subject-term) → **must be aggregated before attaching to student rows** | one row per `TERM_CODE` → no fan-out on term join |\n\nAlternative catalog sources (`CIS_COURSE_CATALOG`, `DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG`) also carry `TOTAL_UNITS` (per `column_concept_total_units` member list) but are **not** in the gold-table set and lack the documented `EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE` regular-term join precedent density of `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED`.\n\nAlternative term source `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL`: retrieved desc states it \"**does not carry IS_REGULAR_TERM**, TERM_STATUS, ADD_DATE or DROP_DATE columns\" → NOT-SUPPORTED for the \"regular academic terms\" requirement.\n\n### 3b. Task-Requirement Fitness Mapping\n\nAtomic requirements decomposed from the question:\n\n| # | Requirement | `SE_PERSON` | `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY` | `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED` | `ACADEMIC_TERMS` | `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL` |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| R1 | filter `EMPLOYEE_TYPE = 'Student'` | **SUPPORTED** (column exists) | NOT-SUPPORTED (no such column) | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED |\n| R2 | filter department code 6 | NOT-SUPPORTED (no dept code column) | **SUPPORTED** (`DEPARTMENT`) | n/a (has `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, but that is the *offering* dept, not the student's) | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED |\n| R3 | filter/output dept name = 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci' | VIOLATES (`ORGANIZATION` uses variant 'Electrical Engineering-Computer Science' — documented in `column_concept_department_name`) | **SUPPORTED** (`DEPARTMENT_NAME` def literally cites this value) | **SUPPORTED** for the *subject* side (`DEPARTMENT_NAME`) | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED |\n| R4 | output MIT ID | **SUPPORTED** | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED |\n| R5 | output full name | **SUPPORTED** (`FULL_NAME`) | **SUPPORTED** (`FULL_NAME`) | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED |\n| R6 | output student year | NOT-SUPPORTED | **SUPPORTED** (`STUDENT_YEAR`) | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED |\n| R7 | running sum of MIT IDs partitioned by student year ordered by MIT ID | **SUPPORTED** (supplies `MIT_ID`) | **SUPPORTED** (supplies `STUDENT_YEAR` partition key) | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED |\n| R8 | measure = total units | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | **SUPPORTED** (`TOTAL_UNITS`) | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED |\n| R9 | scope = \"regular academic terms\" | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED (no regular-term flag) | **SUPPORTED** (`IS_REGULAR_TERM`) | **VIOLATES** (column absent per retrieved desc) |\n| R10 | exclude 'Mathematics' dept on the subject side | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | **SUPPORTED** (`DEPARTMENT_NAME`) | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED |\n| R11 | CV = STDDEV/AVG per department | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | **SUPPORTED** (measure + group key) | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED |\n\nAll four gold tables are required; no single table satisfies the requirement set.\n\n### 3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring\n\n- **\"employee type is 'Student'\"** → lexically anchors to `SE_PERSON.EMPLOYEE_TYPE` (column def \"Employee type classification\"). The hint confirms: `employee type: SE_PERSON.EMPLOYEE_TYPE`, `Student: SE_PERSON.EMPLOYEE_TYPE`. Excludes `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY` (no such column) and `DRUPAL_EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.EMPLOYEE_GROUP` (not in gold set).\n- **\"in department 6\"** → anchors to `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT` (def: \"Academic department code the student belongs to\"). Hint: `department 6: MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT`. Precedents `dw_1983`/`dw_2240` write `t1.DEPARTMENT = '6'` on `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY`. Excludes `SE_PERSON` (documented as carrying no department code).\n- **\"whose department name is 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'\"** → anchors to `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME`, whose retrieved column definition **literally lists 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci' as an example value**. Explicitly excludes `SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION` — `column_concept_department_name` documents that `ORGANIZATION` uses the variant 'Electrical Engineering-Computer Science' for the same unit, so an equality filter there would return zero rows. (Note `dw_463` uses `sp.ORGANIZATION = 'Electrical Engineering-Computer Science'`, confirming the variant.)\n- **\"their MIT ID\"** → `SE_PERSON.MIT_ID` (hint: `MIT ID: SE_PERSON.MIT_ID`); `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY` has no `MIT_ID` column in its retrieved definition.\n- **\"full name\"** → maps **equally** to `SE_PERSON.FULL_NAME` and `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.FULL_NAME` (hint lists both); they are equated by the documented join `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.FULL_NAME <-> SE_PERSON.FULL_NAME`, so the output value is identical either way. Not a discriminating choice.\n- **\"student year\"** → `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.STUDENT_YEAR` (only holder).\n- **\"the running sum of MIT IDs within each student year group ordered by MIT ID\"** → `SUM(MIT_ID) OVER (PARTITION BY STUDENT_YEAR ORDER BY MIT_ID)`. Precedent form confirmed by `dw_3294` (`SUM(t1.ACADEMIC_YEAR) OVER (PARTITION BY t2.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY t1.ACADEMIC_YEAR)`) and `dw_3867` (`SUM(TOTAL_UNITS) OVER (PARTITION BY ACADEMIC_YEAR ORDER BY SUBJECT_ID)`) — both omit an explicit frame clause, i.e. default `RANGE UNBOUNDED PRECEDING → CURRENT ROW`.\n- **\"total units\"** → `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS` (hint: `total units: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS`); `column_concept_total_units` decision guide routes catalog unit statistics to this column.\n- **\"regular academic terms\"** → `ACADEMIC_TERMS.IS_REGULAR_TERM = 'Y'` (hint: `regular academic terms: ACADEMIC_TERMS.IS_REGULAR_TERM`). `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL` is excluded because its retrieved desc states the column is absent.\n- **\"in their department\"** → the student's department, i.e. the CV must be grouped by department name and matched to `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME`. Both `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME` and `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME` share the same academic value domain (per `column_concept_department_name`: \"Catalog, summary, offering, student-directory, and lookup tables store plain department names\"), so a name-equality join is valid.\n- **\"(excluding 'Mathematics')\"** → hint anchors to `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME`, i.e. `<> 'Mathematics'` on the subject side, not on the student side.\n- **\"coefficient of variation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP)\"** → `STDDEV(x) / AVG(x)`. Precedent `dw_4640` writes exactly `STDDEV(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) / NULLIF(AVG(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS), 0) AS coefficient_of_variation`; `dw_2180` writes `STDDEV_SAMP(ss.TOTAL_UNITS) / NULLIF(AVG(ss.TOTAL_UNITS), 0) AS coefficient_of_variation_total_units`. Per the task tip, bare `STDDEV()` is used.\n\n**Ambiguity — `TERM_CODE` vs `EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE`:** the phrase \"subjects **offered in** regular academic terms\" maps lexically to both. The hint lists **both** join keys (`ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE` and `ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE`), so the hint does not disambiguate. The discriminating evidence is (i) the `column_concept_term_code` decision guide, whose `EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE` entry gives the parenthetical example \"**(e.g. regular-term status of the effective term)**\" — a direct match to this task's regular-term filter; and (ii) precedent frequency (see 3d), which favors `EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE`.\n\n### 3d. Precedent Usage Evidence\n\n**CV-of-a-measure precedents (STDDEV/AVG grouped by department):** 2 observed — `dw_4640` (on `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, `GROUP BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `NULLIF(AVG(...),0)`), `dw_2180` (on `SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS`, `GROUP BY ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC`, `NULLIF(AVG(...),0)`). Both attach the CV as a per-group scalar to detail rows via a join.\n\n**`COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED` + `IS_REGULAR_TERM='Y'` join-key precedents:**\n- Via **`EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE`**: 5 — `dw_359` (\"subjects offered in regular terms by the Mathematics department\": `at.TERM_CODE = ccso.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE`), `dw_4061` (\"all subjects offered by the department in regular terms\": `ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE = COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE`), `dw_3417` (\"subjects offered in regular terms\": `ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE = COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE`), `dw_3248` (\"during regular terms\": `t0.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE = t1.TERM_CODE`), `dw_4701` (`at.TERM_CODE = ccso.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE`).\n- Via **`TERM_CODE`**: 3 — `dw_4387` (\"subjects it has ever offered in a regular academic term\": `c.TERM_CODE = t.TERM_CODE`), `dw_3664` (\"subjects offered in regular terms\": `c.TERM_CODE = t.TERM_CODE`), `dw_41` (via `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE = ccso.TERM_CODE`).\n\n**`SE_PERSON` ↔ `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY` join precedents:** 2 — `dw_2759` (`SE_PERSON sp JOIN MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY msd ON sp.FULL_NAME = msd.FULL_NAME`), `dw_463` (same `FULL_NAME` join). Both confirm the hint's join key.\n\n**Course-6 / 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci' student-filter precedents:** 2 — `dw_1983`, `dw_2240`, both writing `WHERE t1.DEPARTMENT = '6' AND t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'` on `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY`.\n\n**Running-sum window precedents (no explicit frame):** 2 — `dw_3294`, `dw_3867`.\n\n## 4. Business Usage\n\n- **`SE_PERSON`**: consumed by `dw_2759` (employee-type × department headcounts, min MIT ID, office-location lists) and `dw_463` (EECS student MIT ID / department averages). Serves \"who is this person and what is their employment classification\" patterns. `LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR` resolves instructors into it via `INSTRUCTOR_NAME = FULL_NAME`.\n- **`MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY`**: consumed by `dw_2759`, `dw_463`, `dw_1983`, `dw_2240`, `dw_1212`, `dw_1033`, `dw_100`, `dw_1350`. Serves per-department student counts, student-year segmentation ('G' graduate), and student contact/office statistics. Its `DEPARTMENT` code is the documented reliable join to `SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE`.\n- **`COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED`**: the most heavily consumed table here — **61 dependent metrics** returned by `metrics_by_table`, spanning unit dispersion (avg/variance/stddev/geometric mean of `TOTAL_UNITS`), HGN-level analysis, grade-type analysis, bulletin flags, term-offering flags, and room/space joins via `MEET_PLACE`. It is the canonical source for catalog-level unit statistics.\n- **`ACADEMIC_TERMS`**: consumed by `dw_359`, `dw_3417`, `dw_4061`, `dw_3248`, `dw_4387`, `dw_3664`, `dw_1049`, `dw_4701`, `dw_2597`, `dw_3294`, `dw_3684`. Serves term-status enrichment/filtering — regular vs non-regular term, previous/current/future, academic-year rollups. It is the exclusive holder of `IS_REGULAR_TERM`, `ADD_DATE`, `DROP_DATE`.\n\n## 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n| Phase 1 entity | `semantic_get` | `semantic_graph` | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `SE_PERSON` | ✅ | ✅ `query_neighbors` both | gold table |\n| `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY` | ✅ | ✅ (via `SE_PERSON` neighbors) | gold table |\n| `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED` | ✅ | ✅ `query_neighbors` joins + `metrics_by_table` (61) | gold table |\n| `ACADEMIC_TERMS` | ✅ | ✅ (via CCSO neighbors) | gold table |\n| `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL` | ✅ (desc via search + CCSO neighbor) | ✅ | excluded — lacks `IS_REGULAR_TERM` |\n| `concept_person_directory` | ✅ | ✅ | |\n| `concept_subject_offering_facts` | ✅ | ✅ | |\n| `concept_academic_term_dimension` | ✅ | ✅ | |\n| `concept_course_catalog_sources` | ✅ | ✅ | |\n| `concept_department_dimension` | ✅ | ✅ | |\n| `column_concept_total_units` | ✅ | ✅ | |\n| `column_concept_department_name` | ✅ | ✅ | |\n| `column_concept_term_code` | ✅ | ✅ | |\n| `column_concept_office_location` | ✅ (desc) | ✅ | not needed for output |\n| `column_concept_year_columns`, `_subject_id`, `_enrollment_measures`, `_master_subject_id`, `_hass_attribute` | ✅ (desc via search) | — | not required by task |\n| Metrics `dw_2759`, `dw_463`, `dw_2240`, `dw_1983`, `dw_4640`, `dw_2180`, `dw_1049`, `dw_3417`, `dw_3294`, `dw_359`, `dw_4061`, `dw_3664`, `dw_4387`, `dw_3248`, `dw_4701`, `dw_2597`, `dw_41`, `dw_1471`, `dw_1335`, `dw_1212`, `dw_3530`, `dw_3684`, `dw_3867` | ✅ full SQL | — | precedent evidence |\n| Non-gold tables from search (`SUBJECT_SUMMARY`, `SUBJECT_OFFERED`, `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY`, `TIP_*`, `LIBRARY_*`, `SIS_*`, `CIS_*`, `DRUPAL_*`, `FCLT_*`, `HR_*`, `SPACE_*`, `TIME_*`, `MOIRA_*`, `IAP_*`, `MASTER_DEPT_*`, etc.) | ✅ desc screened | — | screened out: no `EMPLOYEE_TYPE`, no `STUDENT_YEAR`, no `IS_REGULAR_TERM`, or outside the person/catalog/term domain required |\n\nFacilities/space/building/Moira/IAP entities returned by the broad searches were discarded as completely unrelated (score-driven and semantically disjoint from employee type, student year, and catalog total units).\n\n## 6. Recommendation\n\n### 6a. Recommended tables/columns\n\n| Role | Choice | Justification (evidence) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Employee-type filter | `SE_PERSON.EMPLOYEE_TYPE = 'Student'` | Only table with this column (R1, §3b); hint mapping |\n| Person key / output | `SE_PERSON.MIT_ID`, `SE_PERSON.FULL_NAME` | `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY` has no `MIT_ID` (R4, §3b) |\n| Student dept code filter | `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT = '6'` | Column def + `dw_1983`/`dw_2240` precedent (R2) |\n| Student dept name filter & output | `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'` | Column def cites this exact value; `SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION` uses an incompatible variant (R3, §3c) |\n| Student year output & window partition | `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.STUDENT_YEAR` | Sole holder (R6) |\n| Person↔student join | `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.FULL_NAME = SE_PERSON.FULL_NAME` | Documented graph `joins` edge + `dw_2759`/`dw_463` precedents |\n| Unit measure | `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS` | `column_concept_total_units` decision guide routes catalog unit statistics here (R8) |\n| Subject dept group/exclusion | `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME` (`<> 'Mathematics'`) | Hint anchoring; same academic value domain as the student directory name (§3c) |\n| Regular-term filter | `ACADEMIC_TERMS.IS_REGULAR_TERM = 'Y'` | Exclusive holder; `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL` lacks it (R9) |\n| Term join key | `ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE = COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE` | `column_concept_term_code` decision guide names \"regular-term status of the effective term\" as the `EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE` case; 5-vs-3 precedent majority (§3d) |\n| CV formula | `STDDEV(TOTAL_UNITS) / NULLIF(AVG(TOTAL_UNITS), 0)` | `dw_4640` / `dw_2180` precedent shape; bare `STDDEV()` per task tip |\n| Running sum | `SUM(MIT_ID) OVER (PARTITION BY STUDENT_YEAR ORDER BY MIT_ID)` | `dw_3294` / `dw_3867` precedent shape (no explicit frame) |\n\n### 6b. Recommended SQL writing approach\n\nTwo-CTE/two-level design to avoid fan-out:\n\n1. **`dept_cv` CTE** — aggregate `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED` to **one row per `DEPARTMENT_NAME`**, joining `ACADEMIC_TERMS` on `TERM_CODE = EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE`, filtering `IS_REGULAR_TERM = 'Y'` and `DEPARTMENT_NAME <> 'Mathematics'`, computing `STDDEV(TOTAL_UNITS)/NULLIF(AVG(TOTAL_UNITS),0)`. Aggregating first is essential: the catalog table has many rows per department, so joining it raw to student rows would multiply each student by every subject offering and corrupt the window running sum.\n2. **Main query** — `SE_PERSON` ⋈ `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY` on `FULL_NAME`, filtered to `EMPLOYEE_TYPE='Student'`, `DEPARTMENT='6'`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME='Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'`; then attach the single department-level CV scalar via a name-equality `LEFT JOIN`.\n3. **Window** — `SUM(MIT_ID) OVER (PARTITION BY STUDENT_YEAR ORDER BY MIT_ID)`, default frame (matching precedents).\n4. **SELECT list** — exactly the six requested items, in the asked order: MIT ID, full name, department name, student year, running sum, coefficient of variation. No rounding anywhere.\n5. **Caveats**: (i) `FULL_NAME` is not declared unique in `SE_PERSON` — `dw_463` defends against this with `MIN(MIT_ID)`/`GROUP BY`; here the question asks for per-student rows so no de-duplication is applied, matching `dw_2759`'s plain join. (ii) `LEFT JOIN` on `dept_cv` guarantees student rows survive even if a department had no regular-term catalog offerings (CV would be NULL). (iii) `NULLIF(...,0)` guards division by zero, per both CV precedents.\n\n### 6c. Three-perspective reasons\n\n**Data perspective**\n- `MIT_ID` physically exists only in `SE_PERSON` (retrieved column list); `STUDENT_YEAR` only in `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY`; `EMPLOYEE_TYPE` only in `SE_PERSON`; `TOTAL_UNITS` only in the catalog/offering tables; `IS_REGULAR_TERM` only in `ACADEMIC_TERMS`. All four gold tables are therefore mandatory — no substitution is possible (§3b matrix).\n- `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED` granularity is \"one row per subject offering per term/academic year\" → many rows per department. Pre-aggregating to one row per `DEPARTMENT_NAME` eliminates fan-out against the student grain (\"one row per student\").\n- `ACADEMIC_TERMS` granularity is \"one row per academic term\" → the term join cannot fan out the catalog rows.\n- The `FULL_NAME` join is the only available person↔student link (`MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY` has no `MIT_ID`; `SE_PERSON` has no department code), and it is a documented graph edge.\n- The department-name equality join between `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME` and `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME` is safe because `column_concept_department_name` states both \"store plain department names\" in the same academic domain.\n\n**Semantic-network perspective**\n- `concept_person_directory` explicitly groups `SE_PERSON` and `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY` as jointly answering \"whether they are employee, faculty, or student\" — exactly the R1+R6 combination.\n- `column_concept_department_name`'s decision guide directs student department filtering to `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT`/`DEPARTMENT_NAME` and **warns** that `SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION` uses a different naming variant — ruling out the only plausible alternative for R3.\n- `column_concept_total_units`' decision guide routes \"unit statistics (avg/stddev/variance/geometric mean) over catalog offerings\" to `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS`.\n- `column_concept_term_code`'s decision guide names \"regular-term status of the effective term\" as the `EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE` use case, and its comparison table notes `EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE` \"may differ from the record's TERM_CODE\".\n- `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL`'s retrieved desc states it \"does not carry IS_REGULAR_TERM\" — a hard exclusion for R9.\n- Graph `metrics_by_table` shows 61 metrics depending on `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED`, confirming it as the canonical unit-statistics fact.\n\n**Business perspective**\n- The exact student filter (`DEPARTMENT='6' AND DEPARTMENT_NAME='Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'` on `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY`) appears verbatim in two existing metrics (`dw_1983`, `dw_2240`) — established business phrasing for \"Course 6 EECS students\".\n- The CV-of-a-measure-per-department shape exists as `dw_4640` and `dw_2180`, both computing `STDDEV/NULLIF(AVG,0)` grouped by department and attaching it as a scalar to detail rows — the same task shape.\n- The regular-term catalog unit-statistics shape exists as `dw_359`, `dw_4061`, `dw_3417`, `dw_3248`, `dw_4701` (5 precedents, all via `EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE`) versus `dw_4387`, `dw_3664`, `dw_41` (3 precedents via `TERM_CODE`).\n- The running-sum window shape (no explicit frame clause) exists as `dw_3294` and `dw_3867`.\n- The `SE_PERSON` ⋈ `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY` on `FULL_NAME` pattern exists as `dw_2759` and `dw_463`.\n\n### 6d. Alternatives and tie-breakers\n\n**`TERM_CODE` vs `EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE`** is the only genuinely contested choice; the hint lists both and the question wording (\"subjects offered in regular academic terms\") maps lexically to each.\n\n- *Option A (chosen):* `ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE = COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE`. Supported by the `column_concept_term_code` decision guide's explicit \"regular-term status of the effective term\" example, the `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE` column definition (\"frequently joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE for term-status filtering\"), and a 5-vs-3 precedent majority.\n- *Option B:* `ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE = COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE`. Supported by the decision guide's \"Filtering subject offerings by the term they are offered in → use the fact table's TERM_CODE\" entry, by the literal word \"offered\", and by `dw_4387` whose wording (\"offered in a regular academic term\") is closest to this question's.\n- *Tie-breaker fact that would resolve it:* the row-count/CV-value difference between the two joins for `DEPARTMENT_NAME='Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'` — i.e. how many catalog rows have `TERM_CODE ≠ EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE`. If that set is empty, both options are numerically identical and the choice is moot. **This could not be measured because every `mysql_query` call returned MySQL error 1045 (access denied).** Option A is adopted on the strength of the documented decision-guide example plus precedent majority.\n\n**`SE_PERSON.FULL_NAME` vs `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.FULL_NAME` for the output \"full name\"** — the hint lists both; because the two are equated by the join predicate, the emitted value is identical. `SE_PERSON.FULL_NAME` is used (listed first in the hint). No tie-breaker needed.\n\n**`JOIN` vs `LEFT JOIN` for `dept_cv`** — identical results whenever the EECS department has at least one regular-term catalog offering (expected). `LEFT JOIN` is chosen so student rows are never silently dropped.\n\n---\n\n## Final SQL\n\n> **Verification status:** `mysql_query` could not be executed — every call (6 attempts, including `SELECT 1`) returned `1045 (28000): Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost' (using password: YES)`. The query below is therefore validated against the retrieved column definitions, the semantic-network decision guides, and the SQL of 23 precedent metrics rather than against live data.\n\n```sql\nWITH dept_cv AS (\n    SELECT c.DEPARTMENT_NAME,\n           STDDEV(c.TOTAL_UNITS) / NULLIF(AVG(c.TOTAL_UNITS), 0) AS coefficient_of_variation\n    FROM COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED c\n    JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS t\n      ON t.TERM_CODE = c.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE\n    WHERE t.IS_REGULAR_TERM = 'Y'\n      AND c.DEPARTMENT_NAME <> 'Mathematics'\n    GROUP BY c.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n)\nSELECT p.MIT_ID,\n       p.FULL_NAME,\n       d.DEPARTMENT_NAME,\n       d.STUDENT_YEAR,\n       SUM(p.MIT_ID) OVER (PARTITION BY d.STUDENT_YEAR ORDER BY p.MIT_ID) AS running_sum_mit_id,\n       cv.coefficient_of_variation\nFROM SE_PERSON p\nJOIN MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY d\n  ON d.FULL_NAME = p.FULL_NAME\nLEFT JOIN dept_cv cv\n  ON cv.DEPARTMENT_NAME = d.DEPARTMENT_NAME\nWHERE p.EMPLOYEE_TYPE = 'Student'\n  AND d.DEPARTMENT = '6'\n  AND d.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'\nORDER BY p.MIT_ID;\n```\n\n**Self-check against the question's requested output fields (6, in order):**\n1. MIT ID → `p.MIT_ID` ✅\n2. full name → `p.FULL_NAME` ✅\n3. department name → `d.DEPARTMENT_NAME` ✅\n4. student year → `d.STUDENT_YEAR` ✅\n5. running sum of MIT IDs within each student year group ordered by MIT ID → `SUM(p.MIT_ID) OVER (PARTITION BY d.STUDENT_YEAR ORDER BY p.MIT_ID)` ✅\n6. coefficient of variation (STDDEV, never STDDEV_POP) of total units, regular terms, their department, excluding Mathematics → `cv.coefficient_of_variation` ✅\n\nNo extra columns, no name variants, no `ROUND()` anywhere, bare `STDDEV()` used.\n\n",
